WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.277
One presentation.

00:00:01.277 --> 00:00:02.247
Two audiences.

00:00:02.247 --> 00:00:03.909
A buyer and an operator.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:05.641
Both have ninety seconds.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.342
The buyer needs the problem explained.

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:12.642
The operator needs to see the workflow.

00:00:12.642 --> 00:00:16.890
I change the Gmail brief, while the
required result and disclaimer stay.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.564
HardStop's model turns the request into
ranked preferences.

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:26.733
It favors the problem for the buyer, and
the workflow for the operator.

00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:29.023
Required context stays with the result.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.200
Here's the buyer cut: eighty-five point
six seconds,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.810
with its own matching deck.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.209
The operator cut is eighty-six point two
seconds.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:43.907
Same limit.

00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:45.049
Different content.

00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:46.508
Here's a short excerpt.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
[Excerpt from the original recording]

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.095
The recordings come from Dropbox.

00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:57.238
For each cut, HardStop copies the Google
Slides deck

00:00:57.238 --> 00:01:00.321
and checks that its pages match the
selected clips.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.673
Saved videos are downloaded again and
checked.

00:01:04.673 --> 00:01:08.198
This Gmail draft brings the video and deck
together for review.

00:01:08.198 --> 00:01:09.093
Nothing is sent.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.724
Now ask for thirty seconds.

00:01:13.724 --> 00:01:16.912
The required recordings alone need almost
fifty-four.

00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:19.198
HardStop explains why they cannot fit,

00:01:19.198 --> 00:01:21.604
and preserves the last working delivery.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.978
Harbor uses six new recordings,

00:01:27.978 --> 00:01:30.765
different section names, and a new
dependency.

00:01:30.765 --> 00:01:32.401
After clarifying the brief,

00:01:32.401 --> 00:01:36.945
it produces a forty-three point six-second
cut through the same three apps.

00:01:36.945 --> 00:01:39.065
This is a second fictional example.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:42.602
HardStop.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.723
Change the audience or the time limit,

00:01:44.723 --> 00:01:47.960
and get a video and matching deck you can
review together.
